  "description": "The 2026 election for California's 28th Congressional District pits incumbent Democrat Judy Chu against Republican April Verlato. The district, which spans parts of Los Angeles County including Pasadena, Arcadia, and the San Gabriel Valley, underwent mid-decade redistricting under Proposition 50, changing some of its boundaries. Chu, first elected in 2009 and the first Chinese American woman in Congress, has a strong Democratic voter registration advantage in the district (45% Democratic vs. 23% Republican). The Cook Political Report rates the general election race as 'Solid D,' reflecting the district's heavily Democratic lean. The race was shaped by the January 2025 Eaton Fire that devastated parts of Altadena within the district, and Chu won the June 2 top-two primary with 62.2% of the vote to Verlato's 32.1%.",
